As Business Development Manager (m/f/d) at FlixTrain , you will take full ownership of high-impact projects and partnerships that shape the future of our customer experience.

Driven by a hands-on mindset and a genuine passion for operational excellence, you will identify opportunities, build solutions from the ground up, and continuously push our partners to raise the bar. From managing complex, multi-stakeholder projects to maintaining strong day-to-day partner relationships, you will be the driving force behind seamless, reliable on-board experiences across our growing fleet.

In a rail industry where customer experience increasingly defines the operators of tomorrow, your work will be at the forefront - directly influencing how FlixTrain stays competitive, innovative, and committed to delivering high-quality, memorable journeys for every passenger on board.

About the Role

• Support in defining and executing our strategy to become the largest private and most loved provider of long-distance rail transport

• Drive key strategic projects that enhance the customer experience on board our trains

• Collaborate with a variety of internal and external stakeholders, including production, partner management, and network and business planning

• Establish project management structures, including project timelines and steering formats

• Establish reporting formats (incl. KPI tracking) and prepare presentations for senior management

• You will play an essential role in transforming the transport industry, which will contribute to the long-term success of the company

About You

• Completed degree in business administration, business &amp; logistics, or a related field

• At least 3 years of professional experience in operations consulting or management of cross-functional projects in collaboration with several external partners, preferably in the railway industry

• Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills

• Strong negotiation, communication and presentation skills (incl. PowerPoint)

• A track record of successfully implementing complex projects

• Experience collaborating with internal and external stakeholders

• Self-motivated and reliable, with the drive to continuously improve existing structures

• Full working proficiency in both English and German (both at min. C1 level)

What We Offer&nbsp;

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family. &nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year. &nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : we are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life. &nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members. &nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills. &nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career. &nbsp;

Why Join Flix

At Flix, we focus on making travel easy, safe, and affordable - for both our passengers and our employees. Things move fast here, and there’s plenty of room to make a difference. We’re growing and improving every day, and we need people who are ready to jump in and help shape the way we work.

If&nbsp; you’re looking for a job where you can grow, make an impact, and be part of a team where your effort matters, FlixTrain is the place where you can lead your journey! &nbsp;

